Z||000054||EdsB52||10-29-2001||08:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Reality:<BR><B>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Actually My post is on there before yours so really you had no right to ask the question."<P>Actually dork, if you check the post times you'll see that I was in the middle of writing my post while you were posting your 15 second post. Besides, who are you to decide who has the right to post what? If I wanted to ask a rhetorical question with the knowledge of the existence of your post, I still could.<P>"And i think your being a little harsh on the guy I mean my gosh he was just messing around he probably dosen't need you to jump all over his cause just because he decided to ask if someone besides himself might think that his g/f is cute."<P>I was also messing around and I even alluded to that. Besides, who was that that got his sh!t jumped by many members for posting a pic of his girlfriend a couple months ago? I wasn't involved in that, but many folks were.<P>"I mean shes a little young for my tastes but still shes not hard on the eyes! I understand all the dangers involved with poseing personal items on a national/worldwide forum. I'm sure he does as well."<P>It's not an issue of her looks, just the dangers as you wrote. And if he knows the dangers, well, he must have decided it was worth it. You must think skip-tracing starts and ends at the phone book.<P>"But what you are saying is that you shouldn't trust anyone not even the ones that "we" have all mainly come to call freinds on this forum."<P>Oh yea, I forgot, this club is limited to everyone in the world. Besides, how many members are in this forum are called worse than friends? I'm not one of the cheerleaders in this forum, so I am not considered a friend to all, and other people are as well.<P>"He didn't post his address (yes I know you can just look at the profile page of that person) but hey ... nevermind I'm sure this is a waste of time, I'm young hear me meow!"<P>Again, the skip-tracing comment. If skip-tracers can find hardened criminals hiding out, then I think they can find a kid at home where he or she should be. I'm just saying it's irresponsible, that's all.<P>In summary, if she has low self esteem, as acknowledged, and then she might not have the capacity to forbid him from posting these pics even if she really knew and didn't want them posted. If she's under 16 (in many states) then she doesn't have the legal or emotional capacity to allow or deny him from doing much with her.||||reg||1
